---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts'
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang='en'>
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>🙈 Welcome to The Rebuild of TDN, V5</h1>
			<p>
				A rebuild of tarasis.net a domain I've had since 2002. It has
				nearly always been a blog or landing page; using Wordpress,
				Jeykll, Eleventy, and now Astro (V5 beta).
			</p>
			<p>
				I considered a straight html/css page, but with duplicated
				elements (like blog pages), a desire to make it a more personal
				site inspired by two talks by <a href='https://localghost.dev'
					>Sophie Koonin</a
				>, I decided to have a play with Astro rather than Eleventy and
				play with modern CSS features. The talks I mentioned:

				<ul>
					<li>
						<a href='https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Ks1aIchFiI'
							>"Sophie Koonin - Building websites like it’s 1999…
							in 2022" - State of the Browser</a
						>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href='https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2ZUqa-lTbnU'
							>"Sophie Koonin – This Website Is under
							Construction, a Love Letter to the Personal Website"
							– btconf</a
						>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
			<p>
				Who am I? Robert McGovern. 48yo confused man who is struggling
				to work, dealing with depression, and currently struggling with
				alcoholism. So as part of my process of recovery I am going to
				be working on a rebuild of this site, and "do it in public".
				Although not streamed :)
			</p>
			<p>
				I've made some concious choices that I want to:
				<ul>
					<li>Multi theme switcher</li>
					<li>Use YAML rather than JSON for some data files</li>
					<li>
						While I can use remapping of frontmatter on older blog
						posts, I am going to redo some of frontmatter
					</li>
					<li>
						The blog will not just be about tech stuff, it will
						include notes, and stuff about health, depression
						alcoholism and other struggles
					</li>
					<li>
						Explore pulling in data from Spotify and other APIs, so
						the page reflects more me
					</li>
					<li>I want to have a /now page.</li>
					<li>Link to / list work I've done</li>
					<li>Bring in fav photos, or most recent ones</li>
				</ul>
				So yes, its going to be a bit busy but hopefully not cluttered.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
